 resolution / `uv sync --extra eval` / `make test` — none exercise outputConfig against the resolved botocore, so a too-low floor would ship undetected here and surface as ParamValidationError in the downstream wire-feature ticket.","Environment probe: installed botocore/boto3 versions are not readable via repo-scoped tools (path outside snapshot root), so the boundary is also not confirmable from the environment."],"finding":"The floor version botocore>=1.43.0 is asserted as the version that ADDS outputConfig support, but the plan's only cited evidence (the E1 experiment) establishes only that botocore 1.40.61 REJECTS outputConfig with ParamValidationError — it does not confirm that 1.43.0 is the first version that ACCEPTS it. This is a Partially-verified external-capability boundary the entire ticket depends on.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9f488828e0149c89","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context/Problem (\"The wire feature needs botocore >= 1.43\") and Approach (\"Add an explicit floor botocore>=1.43.0\")","norm_id":"necab08a10fd7ceeb","priority":0.4889,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["outputConfig was actually added in a botocore later than 1.43.0 (e.g., 1.44); this ticket's lock succeeds and make test passes, but the downstream capability-rows ticket still hits ParamValidationError with no diagnostic pointing back here.","The exact accepting version is 1.42.x (below the proposed floor), in which case the floor is stricter than needed and needlessly narrows the resolvable version window against the eval-fork cap."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_ex